ist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000110465921026162/0001104659-21-026162-index.htm","tone":"warn"},{"date":"2021-02-22","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000110465921026160/0001104659-21-026160-index.htm","tone":"warn"},{"date":"2021-02-17","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000110465921024878/0001104659-21-024878-index.htm","tone":"warn"}],"summary":{"sentences":["Butterfly Network, Inc. files with the SEC under \"X-Ray Apparatus & Tubes & Related Irradiation Apparatus\", based in MA, and has been publicly reporting for 5 years.","It reported $104.0m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 39.5% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 71.4%.","Listed on NYSE, it is still consuming cash, with roughly 27 months of runway at the current burn."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 39.5% year on year (Q2 2026 vs Q2 2025), reaching $32.6m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000180417626000027/0001804176-26-000027-index.htm","accession":"0001804176-26-000027"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000180417626000027/0001804176-26-000027-index.htm","accession":"0001804176-26-000027"},{"text":"Gross margin of 71.4% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000180417626000027/0001804176-26-000027-index.htm","accession":"0001804176-26-000027"},{"text":"Gross margin expanded from 63.7% to 71.4% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000180417626000027/0001804176-26-000027-index.htm","accession":"0001804176-26-000027"},{"text":"Net cash of $199.9m against total assets of $283.0m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000180417626000027/0001804176-26-000027-index.htm","accession":"0001804176-26-000027"}],"bear":[{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-41.9% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000180417626000027/0001804176-26-000027-index.htm","accession":"0001804176-26-000027"},{"text":"About 27 months of cash at the current burn ($199.9m against $89.5m a year). A company that must raise is a company that raises on the buyer's terms.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000180417626000016/0001804176-26-000016-index.htm","accession":"0001804176-26-000016"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 5.5% over the year (Q2 2026 vs Q2 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000180417626000027/0001804176-26-000027-index.htm","accession":"0001804176-26-000027"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 41.9% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (8,454,198 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1804176/000110465926086681/0001104659-26-086681-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 63.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.63,"consecutive":2,"current":0.714,"current_display":"71.4%","threshold_display":"63.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 20.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.2,"consecutive":2,"current":0.395,"current_display":"39.5%","threshold_display":"20.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":26.806,"current_display":"27 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"rationale":"Below twelve months the company raises on whatever terms it can get, and that dilution lands on you.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 13.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.13,"consecutive":1,"current":0.055,"current_display":"5.5%","threshold_display":"13.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.0,"current_display":"0.00","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"